<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46956" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦμαρ</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		 and <i><span class="en">
			Arc.
		</span></i>
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἆμαρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμέρα</span>
			, <i>day</i>, the prevailing form in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύκτες τε καὶ ἤματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.183
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νύκτας τε καὶ ἦμαρ</span> by
			night and <i>day</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.490
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.63
			</span></i> (where sg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦμαρ</span> is used as
			pl., as in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποσσῆμαρ, ἐννῆμαρ, ἑξῆμαρ</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">; ἆμαρ ἢ νύκτες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					4.256
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦμαρ</span> alone, <i>by
			day</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				176
			</span></i> (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἦ</span>. <i>on that
				day</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>JHS</u>
				12.234
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cilicia</span>)); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέσον ἦ</span>. mid<i>day</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				21.111
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				9.113
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δείελον ἦ</span>.
			evening, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.606
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤματι χειμερίῳ</span> on a
			winter's <i>day</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				12.279
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				16.385
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> used in 
				Ep.
			 with Adjs., of a state or condition, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴσιμον, ὀλέθριον, μόρσιμον, νηλεὲς
			ἦ</span>., <i>the day</i> of destiny, of death, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				8.72
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				19.294
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				10.175
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.484
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλεύθερον, δούλιον, ἀναγκαῖον
				ἦ</span>., <i>the day</i> of freedom, of slavery, <i><span class="en">
				6.455
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				463
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				16.836
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόστιμον ἦ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.9
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ. ὀρφανικόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					22.490
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> with Preps.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἤματι</span>
			<i>day by day, daily</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				12.105
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				14.105
			</span></i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰὲν ἐπ᾽ ἤματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					688
				</span></i>
			); <i>in a day, within a day's space</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.48
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				19.229
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				2.284
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἄματι</span>”
				<i>at the close of day</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					24.139
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἆ</span>. <i>by day</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				199
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἦ</span>. <i>for a
			day</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				255.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				401
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ἆμαρ ἕκαστον, ἆμαρ ἐπ᾽
				ἆμαρ</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				17.96
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				11.69
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦ. ἐπ᾽ ἦ. ἀεί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.499
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἦ</span>. <i>day by
			day</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				798
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				628
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἦ. αἰεί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>OC</u>
					682
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀεὶ κατ᾽ ἦ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				392
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀεὶ τὸ κατ᾽ ἦ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>El.</u>
				145
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κατ᾽ ἆμαρ</span>
			<i>the needs of the day, one's daily bread</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1089
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				593
			</span></i>(lyr.); but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ᾽ ἆ</span>. also,
				<i>this day, to-day</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>OC</u>
				1079
			</span></i>,cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Aj.</u>
				753
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μὲν παρ᾽ ἆ., τὸ δέ</span>
			<i>on one day, and on the next . . </i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				11.63
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρ᾽ ἦ</span>. <i>on the
			morrow</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1455
			</span></i>(lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρ᾽ ἦ. ἡμέρα</span> day
				<i>after day</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				475
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰν ἄματα πάντα</span>”
				<i>in perpetuity,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					IG
					5(2).5
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Tegea</span>); without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰν</span>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				262.22
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Mantinea</span>).</div>
